18.github.io\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code as a Daily Driver</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-tutorial\">tutorial</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">A deep dive into using Claude Code as a daily driver, covering Claude.md files, Skills, Subagents, Plugins, and Model Context Protocol (MCP) integrations.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">arps18</span> · <span class=\"source\">HN</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">llms</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://orchidfiles.com\" target=\"_blank\">I'm Tired of Talking to AI</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">A personal reflection on AI fatigue and the changing nature of human-computer interaction as AI assistants become more prevalent in daily workflows.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">theorchid</span> · <span class=\"source\">HN</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-fatigue</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">opinion</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\"