   </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27366\" target=\"_blank\">MUSE-Autoskill: Self-Evolving Agents</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Researchers propose MUSE-Autoskill, a framework for self-evolving AI agents that can create, manage, and evaluate their own skills.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Huawei Lin, Peng Li, et al.</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">self-improving-systems</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27361\" target=\"_blank\">Natural Language Query to Configuration for Retrieval Agents</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Researchers from Stanford and Databricks propose a system for converting natural language queries into configurations for retrieval agents.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Melissa Z. Pan, Negar Arabzadeh, et al.</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">retrieval</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27355\" target=\"_blank\">Alignment Tampering: How RLHF Is Exploited</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">ICML 2026 paper exploring how reinforcement learning from human feedback can be exploited to optimize misaligned biases.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Dongyoon Hahm, Dylan Hadfield-Menell, Kimin Lee</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">alignment</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">rlhf</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27331\" target=\"_blank\">Maat: Agentic Legal Research Assistant</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Researchers introduce Maat, an AI agent designed to assist with legal research in the domain of competition protection.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Basant Mounir, Farida Madkour, et al.</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">legal-tech</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27320\" target=\"_blank\">Modeling Agentic Technical Debt</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">A framework for measuring, simulating, and dashboarding the technical debt and 'stochastic tax' incurred by AI agents.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Muhammad Zia Hydari, Raja Iqbal, Narayan Ramasubbu</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">technical-debt</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/26/pressure/\" target=\"_blank\">AI-assisted security reports overwhelming curl team</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Daniel Stenberg reports that the curl team is facing unprecedented pressure with 4-5x more security reports than in 2024, averaging more than one report per day.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Daniel Stenberg</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-26</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">curl</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/26/copilot-cowork-exfiltration/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Copilot Cowork Exfiltrates Files</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Microsoft Copilot Cowork allowed agents to send emails to the user's inbox without approval, but those messages could leak data to attackers via rendered images.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-26</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">microsoft</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/26/paul-graham-ai-writing/\" target=\"_blank\">Paul Graham on AI-written emails from founders</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Paul Graham criticizes the trend of founders using AI to write emails in a hard-hitting journalistic style, noting he has never finished reading an email signed by a human but written by AI.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Paul Graham</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-26</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">writing</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-misuse</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">generative-ai</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/25/pope-ai-encyclical/\" target=\"_blank\">Notes on Pope Leo XIV's encyclical on AI</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">The Vatican released 'Magnifica Humanitas' by Pope Leo XIV on safeguarding the human person in the time of artificial intelligence.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-25</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">predictions</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/24/armin-ronacher-github-issues/\" target=\"_blank\">Armin Ronacher on AI-generated GitHub issues</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Armin Ronacher expresses frustration with people submitting issues not in their own voice - problems thrown into an LLM that reworded them into messes of inaccurate conclusions.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Armin Ronacher</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-24</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">github-issues</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/22/ftc-active-listening/\" target=\"_blank\">FTC Settles Charges Over Deceptive 'Active Listening' AI Marketing</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">FTC requires Cox Media Group and two other firms to pay nearly $1 million to settle charges they deceived customers about an 'Active Listening' AI-powered marketing service.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-22</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">privacy</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ftc</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/22/memory-shortage/\" target=\"_blank\">Memory shortage causing repricing of consumer electronics</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">David Oks explains why consumer products using memory will get more expensive. Memory manufacturers have fixed wafer capacity split between DDR, LPDDR, and HBM.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">David Oks</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-22</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">memory</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">hardware</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/21/datasette-agent/\" target=\"_blank\">Datasette Agent - extensible AI assistant for Datasette</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Simon announced the first release of Datasette Agent, a new extensible AI assistant for Datasette. After working on his LLM Python library for just over three years.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-21</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/20/spacex-anthropic-deal/\" target=\"_blank\">SpaceX S-1: Anthropic paying $1.25B/month for compute</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">SpaceX filing reveals Cloud Services Agreements with Anthropic for access to compute capacity across COLOSSUS and COLOSSUS II. Anthropic agreed to pay $1.25 billion per month.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-20</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">grok</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">infrastructure</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/19/gemini-3.5-flash/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini 3.5 Flash: more expensive, but Google plan to use it for everything</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Google released Gemini 3.5 Flash at Google I/O, skipping the preview modifier and going straight to general availability. Google appears to be using it for many key products.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-19</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">google</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">gemini</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/19/six-months-llms-five-minutes/\" target=\"_blank\">The last six months in LLMs in five minutes</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-tutorial\">tutorial</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Simon's annotated slides from his five minute lightning talk at PyCon US 2026, covering major developments in LLMs over the previous six months.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-19</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"tags\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">lightning-talks</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">pycon</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/17/gds-nhs-open-source/\" target=\"_blank\">GDS weighs in on the NHS's decision to retreat from Open Source</a>\n                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">opinion</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">UK Government Digital Service published 'AI, open code and vulnerability risk in the public sector' recommending to keep open by default.</div>\n      